  const V182_BIOS=["Regional manager, self-appointed action hero, and the only man who can turn shouting PARKOUR into a three-stop teleport itinerary.", "A snowman with no survival instinct, no fear of summer, and a deeply concerning amount of optimism.", "A starfish whose tactical plan is usually wrong, loud, and somehow still effective.", "A goat who regards fences as suggestions and personal space as a rumor started by cowards.", "Throws glowing cards because regular playing cards apparently were not dramatic enough for New Orleans.", "Brings enough hearts to solve a friendship problem or create several entirely new problems.", "Small, yellow, numerous, and permanently one banana away from a workplace incident.", "He saw a Goomba launcher on the job posting and immediately asked about dental benefits.", "Defends the universe with mint, berries, and powers that sound like they were invented during recess.", "Moves so smoothly that enemies briefly forget they are supposed to be attacking him.", "A Space Ranger with a laser, a mission, and absolutely no evidence that Star Command approved any of this.", "Has perfected the art of looking disappointed while a personal rain cloud ruins everyone else's afternoon.", "Has been ignored for so long that becoming enormous now feels less like a power and more like reasonable escalation.", "Would prefer snacks and a nap, but ghosts apparently keep getting added to the syllabus.", "Has a headache, no plan, and enough psychic energy to make those first two facts everybody else's problem.", "A doctor in the same way a vending machine is a nutritionist: technically present and wildly unqualified.", "Calm, capable, and dramatically overqualified for a roster where breakfast cereal can fight back.", "Every field trip begins with curiosity and ends with someone asking whether the bus is insured for interdimensional travel.", "Sells propane, propane accessories, and increasingly difficult explanations for why the propane is weaponized.", "There are no defeated enemies, only happy little accidents that wandered too close to the eraser.", "Nobody knows exactly what Grimace is, which is probably why nobody is brave enough to question the fries.", "Two times the size, one-star speed, and exactly the amount of subtlety expected from a nuclear lizard with an Atomic Blast.", "Can find the map, the backpack, and apparently the precise coordinates of anyone who needs to be blasted with a star.", "Part basketball legend, part cactus, and entirely the reason the desert waiver is six pages long.", "A sheriff who settled the old 'reach for the sky' problem by bringing a lasso to a platformer.", "Lets the wind do the talking, the leaves do the fighting, and everyone else do the explaining.", "Royalty with a combat strategy best summarized as 'be faster than the thing you are pouncing on.'", "Wanted a quiet factory job and instead became the shortest member of upper management with an attack animation.", "Hard shell, soft center, and now recharges quickly enough to make every candy aisle nervous.", "Spent centuries forging the One Ring, then discovered the Action button and immediately revised the entire battle plan.", "Has super speed, heat vision, and the growing suspicion that this assignment is below her pay grade.", "Would like everyone to chill. Unlike your uncle at Thanksgiving, he has the equipment to enforce it.", "A glider-riding menace who looked at Green Goblin and decided the costume needed even less restraint.", "Has protected the rainbow for decades and is no longer accepting cereal-related apologies.", "Can become almost anyone, which makes the character-selection screen an administrative nightmare.", "Tiny arms. Massive feet. Zero interest in hearing why stomping is not a complete conflict-resolution strategy.", "One never stops talking, the other breathes fire, and somehow Dragon remains the easier roommate.", "Delegates nearly everything to flying monkeys, proving villainy also understands middle management.", "Can communicate disappointment at a distance, which is fortunate because nobody wants to stand close enough to ask for clarification.", "Does not need stats. Stats need Chuck Norris and are afraid to admit it.", "A rotating committee of quarterbacks united by one shared superpower: making every pass feel historically significant.", "Has survived prehistoric appliances, Fred Flintstone, and now whatever insurance claim Dino Spin creates.", "A mysterious paper-bag hero whose greatest power may be convincing New York that this counts as a disguise.", "Karate confidence, pink velocity, and exactly zero interest in waiting for the other person to finish speaking.", "Wanted to be a dentist. Naturally, the next career step was weaponizing oral hygiene.", "When your tactical backup is a dragon, most meetings become very short.", "Professor by day. Questionable superhero by slightly later that same day. Dr. T weaponizes extra credit, ignores reasonable office-hour boundaries, and has somehow discovered the academic secret to temporary flight.", "Believes every conflict can be solved by sharing a heart, preferably at projectile speed.", "A ghost made mostly of slime, bad manners, and the confidence that walls are somebody else's problem.", "Usually Butters. Occasionally Professor Chaos. Never a situation the adults of South Park are prepared to handle.", "Carries crayons, glue-adjacent energy, and the unsettling confidence of a child who has absolutely misunderstood the assignment.", "A storage solution that finally snapped and chose projectile-based organization.", "Groundskeeper, leaf-blower enthusiast, and living proof that Scottish rage is a renewable energy source.", "Has too many cats, not enough supervision, and a throwing arm that has become a municipal concern.", "A suburban mother who discovered force fields and immediately upgraded family conflict resolution to magical containment.", "Snack-cake royalty with the unsettling ability to turn lunchbox nostalgia into an area-of-effect problem."];
