    // Funny dossier pass for every actual character.
    const V202_BIOS={"Ahsoka Tano": "Calm, capable, and dramatically overqualified for a roster where breakfast syrup can develop opinions.", "Amy": "Arrives with a heart, a hammer-sized amount of confidence, and absolutely no indoor voice.", "Bob Ross": "There are no defeated enemies—only happy little accidents with a suspicious amount of eraser dust.", "Bombastic Bag-Man": "Spider-Man’s laundry day went badly enough to become a full-time identity.", "Browns QBs 99–26": "Twenty-seven quarterbacks enter. One football leaves in a direction nobody charted.", "Butters": "One-star everything until Professor Chaos clocks in and HR quietly leaves the building.", "Buzz": "Space Ranger, toy, laser enthusiast, and still waiting for Star Command to answer one email.", "Chuck Norris": "No dossier needed. The dossier asked Chuck Norris for permission to exist.", "Crazy Cat Lady": "Carries no weapon because apparently Springfield has an unlimited supply of throwable cats.", "Daenerys": "Solves tactical problems by outsourcing them to a dragon. Hard to argue with the workflow.", "Donkey + Dragon": "One never stops talking. The other breathes fire. Somehow the fire-breather is the quieter one.", "Dora": "Can locate anything except whoever approved giving her combat responsibilities.", "Dr. Trendowski": "Professor by day. Questionable superhero by slightly later that same day. Dr. T weaponizes extra credit, ignores reasonable office-hour boundaries, and has somehow discovered the academic secret to temporary flight.", "Eeyore": "Moves at the speed of mild disappointment and weaponizes weather to match the mood.", "Gambit": "A professional card enthusiast who discovered glowing playing cards shorten most meetings.", "Godzilla": "A skyscraper-sized reminder that cardio is optional when the city has nowhere else to go.", "Grimace": "Nobody knows exactly what Grimace is. The fries have stopped asking.", "Groundskeeper Willie": "Discovered that a leaf blower works considerably better when pointed directly at the problem.", "Hank Hill": "Sells propane, propane accessories, and apparently propane-based conflict resolution.", "Hermey": "Wanted to be a dentist. Somehow that became giant teeth erupting from the ground.", "Hobgoblin": "Took one look at a normal commute and decided a flaming glider was the responsible option.", "Larry": "The only employee who heard “Goomba launcher” and asked about advancement opportunities.", "Little Debbie": "She brought snacks. Unfortunately, they have a blast radius.", "Little Green Man": "Has spent his entire life waiting for The Claw and is now wildly overqualified to operate it.", "Lucky": "Has defended one cereal bowl for decades and still treats every rainbow incident as personal.", "Granny": "Sweet, patient, and armed with the original social network. Old School Twitter sends Tweety across the screen to daze regular enemies for six seconds while bosses take one point of damage.", "Meg": "Has endured enough disrespect to justify becoming enormous whenever she feels like it.", "Michael Jackson": "Can defeat enemies while making everyone else look painfully under-rehearsed.", "Michael Scott": "Parkour is not a skill here. It is a management philosophy with collision damage.", "Minion": "Small, yellow, numerous, and somehow still trusted around industrial equipment.", "Mint-Berry Crunch": "Possesses the power of mint, berries, and a résumé nobody has successfully verified.", "Miss Piggy": "Karate-adjacent confidence delivered with enough pink velocity to become a weather event.", "Mr. Freeze": "Would like everyone to chill, and unlike most people who say that, can enforce it.", "Mrs. Butterworth": "Breakfast’s most polite arms dealer. She fires a syrup Hadouken straight ahead and lets the projectile do the sticky work.", "Ms. Frizzle": "Field-trip policy: seatbelts optional, laws of physics negotiable, learning mandatory.", "Mystique": "The character-select screen’s worst possible identity-verification problem.", "Nala": "Royalty with the subtle combat philosophy of simply launching herself at the issue.", "Olaf": "A snowman whose confidence remains completely unaffected by the existence of summer.", "Oompa Loompa": "OSHA requested several meetings. The chocolate department declined all of them.", "Patrick": "Tactical awareness of a throw pillow. Commitment of a wrecking ball.", "Pocahontas": "Paints with all the colors of the wind, but mostly uses them to throw leaves at people.", "Psyduck": "Has a headache, has no idea what is happening, and remains alarmingly dangerous.", "Ralph Wiggum": "Has eaten enough crayons to weaponize them. This is somehow one of his better school decisions.", "Randall": "A goat who has never seen a boundary he did not immediately classify as optional.", "Red M&M": "Hard shell, soft center, zero interest in resolving conflict diplomatically.", "Sauron": "Spent centuries looking for one ring, then discovered the F key and reprioritized.", "Scooby": "Would prefer a sandwich, but supernatural crowd control is apparently part of the job.", "Shaq(tis)": "Part basketball legend, part cactus problem, entirely difficult to explain.", "Share Bear": "Weaponizes kindness so aggressively that even the hearts have splash damage.", "Slimer": "A floating health-code violation with the social boundaries of an unlocked refrigerator.", "Snape": "Looks disappointed in you before the level even finishes loading.", "Stay Puft": "A cheerful marshmallow skyscraper who moves like a parade float and hits like a zoning disaster.", "Supergirl": "Can fly, has heat vision, and somehow got assigned the same review game as everyone else.", "T-Rex": "Arms too short for most tasks. Feet perfectly sized for ending arguments.", "T-Rex (Jurassic Park)": "Arms too short for most tasks. Feet perfectly sized for ending arguments.", "Tupperware": "Throws storage containers at evil and presumably labels the leftovers afterward.", "Wicked Witch": "Has flying monkeys because walking over to solve a problem personally is for amateurs.", "Wilma": "Survived prehistoric appliances, Fred Flintstone, and now combat by dinosaur spin cycle.", "Woody": "A sheriff who upgraded from a pull-string voice box to pulling enemies across the screen.", "Zoidberg": "A doctor in the same way a gas-station hot dog is a balanced meal."};
